# GitHub self-hosted runners

When the ask is self-hosted Actions runners (register, labels, `runs-on`),
stay in the `github` plugin. Do not invent a dedicated runners plugin.

## Workflow YAML

- Prefer labels the repo already uses (`runs-on: [self-hosted, linux, x64]`
  or the project’s exact set) — never invent label taxonomies.
- Keep secrets out of workflow files (`github-actions`); runner tokens are
  registration-time only and never committed.
- Soft-fail or route jobs when self-hosted capacity is optional — match
  neighboring workflows.

## Runner ops

1. Never invent runner names, group ids, or org/repo targets — list/resolve
   via GitHub MCP/`gh` first.
2. Registration tokens are short-lived secrets — do not paste them into chat
   or commits (`security-secrets` posture).
3. Remove/offline a runner or widen runner group access needs an explicit
   verb naming the runner or group.
4. Prefer ephemeral / just-in-time patterns when the project already uses
   them; do not silently switch to persistent privileged runners.

## Pairing

- `github-actions` — workflow structure and pins
- `github-ci-from-main` — changes that must land on the default branch
- `github-pr-checks` — prove a run picked up the runner label
